   "failure_scenario": "A candidate preview continuously emits output without newlines. The shared daemon retains that output indefinitely and can exhaust its memory, stopping the factory.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"${TMPDIR%/}/preview-adjudication.K61FKn/memory.ts\"",
    "output": "Real Seatbelt; temporary script starts an actual preview, emits 33,554,432 bytes after readiness, and measures heap after garbage collection:\nnewline=true: before=2985012, after=2722382, retainedHeapDelta=-262630\nnewline=false: before=3389216, after=36416161, retainedHeapDelta=33026945"
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD preview.ts installs persistent onStdoutLine/onStderrLine callbacks with tailLimit: 4_000. In proc.ts:324-340, lineSplitter executes `pending += chunk` and retains pending until newline or stream closure; the tail limit and collect's `.slice(-4_000)` do not bound this buffer. At base, preview.ts:205-210 collected raw chunks using `output = (output + chunk.toString()).slice(-4_000)`. The unbounded splitter predates this change, but the change exposes it to persistent preview output."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A candidate's preview server prints output that never ends a line, such as a long progress spinner, a binary blob or a deliberate flood. The daemon then holds all of that output in memory for as long as the preview runs, so its memory grows without limit and can take down the daemon that every other run shares.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $SCRATCH/f1/repro.ts nonl; bun $SCRATCH/f1/repro.ts nl  (startPreview under fakeConfinement; after readiness, serve writes 32 x 1 MiB to stdout, with or without a trailing newline per chunk, then sleeps; heapUsed measured after forced GC)",
    "output": "nonl heap delta bytes: 33618600\nnl heap delta bytes: 1116105"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, serve runs through runConfined with onStdoutLine/onStderrLine: collect (preview.ts:181-193). runSandboxed always installs its own onStdoutLine to detect the start token. lineSplitter in proc.ts:324-341 does `pending += chunk` and only trims it at a newline, and neither tailLimit nor collect's slice(-4000) limits `pending`. Serve has no timeout, so the buffer lives for the whole preview. At base, serve was a raw spawn with `output = (output + chunk.toString()).slice(-4_000)`, which stayed bounded."
  }
 },
